## Evidence

Open work migrated from the canonical TODO. Add implementation and
validation evidence here as the task advances.

A corpus probe against the current lawful source installation narrowed the
`ui-images` semantic blocker class without relaxing its conversion policy. All
431 blocked packages contain one extracted `p3d-sprite` JSON member rather than
a physical raster, so the existing direct-texture gate is behaving correctly.

- 353 of the 431 package roots have a sibling source PNG beside the owning P3D.
- 308 of those PNGs exactly match the sprite-declared `image_size` dimensions.
- 45 sibling PNGs have different dimensions, and 78 packages have no sibling
  PNG, so neither group is eligible for automatic promotion from this evidence.
- The generated Pure3D contract declares `tlSpriteChunk` with one child
  `image` chunk, while the current extractor publishes only the sprite wrapper
  JSON.

The next implementation boundary is a verified raster-authority catalog, not a
planner heuristic. It must bind package identity, sprite evidence, raster path,
byte count, SHA-256, and dimensions before any matching package is promoted to
`Texture2D`; unmatched or dimension-conflicting packages must remain semantic
blockers.

The embedded-sprite extraction boundary is now implemented and corpus-proven.
Commit `00bf92ac` publishes each sprite-owned `IMAGE_DATA` payload with exact
ancestry and digest while deliberately leaving DDS behind the semantic compiler
gate.

- All 431 blocked UI-image P3Ds publish 4,083 DDS tiles with zero byte, digest,
  ordinal, or parent mismatches; the tiles contain 39,368,064 source bytes.
- The corpus uses DXT1, DXT3, and DXT5 DDS payloads. Every sprite's declared
  `image_count` equals its actual direct `IMAGE` child count.
- A reconstruction probe against all 308 exact-dimension sibling PNG references
  found one structural rule with zero grid failures: flip each decoded tile on
  Y, arrange the repeated tile grid row-major, overlap adjacent tiles by
  `2 * blit_border`, then crop the result to `image_size`.
- Across those 308 references, alpha mean-absolute error has median 0.10/255 and
  maximum 0.235/255. Premultiplied RGB error has median 1.95/255 and maximum
  6.17/255; all 308 combined errors are below 10/255 and 302 are below 5/255.
- Independently of sibling PNGs, that grid derivation succeeds for all 431
  sprites with zero structural failures. Every sprite uses `blit_border=1`,
  across eight rectangular grid shapes.

The next semantic compiler must implement deterministic BC1/DXT1, BC2/DXT3,
and BC3/DXT5 decode plus that source-derived tile assembly. Sibling PNG files
remain comparison evidence only and must not become reconstruction inputs or
ownership heuristics.

Commit `2363a5b0` now implements the source-derived raster core without using
sibling PNG files as inputs. The `p3d` crate accepts only the corpus-proven
single-level legacy DDS subset and fails closed on unsupported or ambiguous
variants.

- The decoder supports DXT1, DXT3, and DXT5 only. Representative lawful-source
  tiles for all three formats decode byte-for-byte identically to Pillow RGBA.
- The assembler requires exactly one structural grid, flips each decoded tile
  on Y, overlaps adjacent tiles by `2 * blit_border`, and crops to `image_size`.
- Running the actual Rust decoder and assembler across all 431 sprite packages
  assembled all 4,083 tiles with zero structural failures and 39,368,064 DDS
  source bytes consumed.
- The 308 exact-dimension PNG comparisons retained the earlier independent
  measurements: alpha error median 0.10/255 and maximum 0.235/255, with
  premultiplied RGB median 1.95/255 and maximum 6.17/255.

The remaining UI-image compiler boundary is artifact publication and package
promotion. It must encode the assembled source-backed RGBA raster into a
canonical importable artifact, bind that artifact to package provenance, and
only then replace the current `SemanticSource` plan with `Texture2D` import.
